# minimum required Qore version
%requires qore >= 2.0
%modern
# allow the weak reference operator (:=)
%allow-weak-references

%requires(reexport) DataProvider >= 3.8
%requires(reexport) TypeScriptProxy
%requires ConnectionProvider
%requires ProviderIndexUtil
%requires RestClient
%requires RestClientIo
%requires Swagger
%requires OpenApi3
%requires RestSchemaDataProvider
%requires FileLocationHandler
%requires FsUtil
%requires Util
%requires Logger
%requires AsyncSocketIo
%requires GoogleDataProvider

%requires json
%requires process
%requires v8
%requires yaml
%requires uuid

module TypeScriptActionInterface {
    version = "1.1";
    desc = "User module providing an API for Qore DataProvider app actions in TypeScript";
    author = "David Nichols <david@qore.org>";
    url = "http://qore.org";
    license = "MIT";
    init = sub () {
        # Publish a lightweight exact identity inventory for qualified index discovery.
        DataProviderActionCatalog::registerDiscoveryInventoryProvider(
            TypeScriptActionInterface::DiscoveryInventoryProviderName,
            \TypeScriptActionInterface::getDiscoveryInventory());

        # Register the module's initializer
        DataProvider::registerStaticInitializer(\TypeScriptActionInterface::init());

        # Register the data provider factory
        DataProvider::registerFactory(new TypeScriptActionDataProviderFactory());

        # initialize apps with deferred action initialization
        TypeScriptActionInterfacePriv::init();
    };
}

%ifdef QoreDebug
public sub ASSERT(*softbool b) {
    if (!b) {
        throw "ASSERTION-FAILED", "assertion failed";
    }
}
%else
public sub ASSERT(*softbool b) {}
%endif

/** @mainpage TypeScriptActionInterface Module

    @tableofcontents

    @section typescriptactioninterfaceintro TypeScriptActionInterface Module Introduction

    @anchor TypeScriptActionInterfaceintro

    The %TypeScriptActionInterface module provides a @ref dataproviderintro "data provider" and app action API for
    TypeScript code.

    @section TypeScriptActionInterface_relnotes Release Notes

    Generic API calls preserve the app-specific synchronous client's authentication and request policies,
    including HubSpot CMS grant checks and AWS request signing, for both app roots and child providers.

    @subsection TypeScriptActionInterface_v1_1 TypeScriptActionInterface v1.1
    - Bulk app initialization retains each app's failure and continues registering the remaining apps;
      direct app/action initialization still raises the original error. HubSpot's
      \c HUBSPOT-SCHEMAS-UNAVAILABLE error now preserves its identity, connection scheme, and OAuth2 metadata
      just like \c APP-SCHEMAS-UNAVAILABLE, while its actions retain the schema error and remediation.
    - schema cache filenames use a fixed-length SHA-256 digest of the schema location and canonical allowed-path
      set, so long snapshot locations no longer exceed filesystem filename limits. Path order and duplicates
      share one entry, and paths containing commas cannot collide with multiple separate paths. Old cache
      filenames are ignored and entries are regenerated on first use; see \c design/schema-cache.md.
    - schema-backed requests preserve percent-encoded path/query values without encoding them twice;
      requests containing only path variables pass an empty object to request conversion callbacks
    - Apps reporting \c APP-SCHEMAS-UNAVAILABLE now register their identity, REST connection scheme, and OAuth2
      metadata while retaining structured failures for deferred actions. A synchronous \c schema_metadata callback
      refreshes failed snapshot selections on retry; successfully selected snapshots remain pinned until restart.
      TypeScriptActionInterface::getAppSchemaError() exposes the last schema error without blocking connections.
      Other initialization errors still fail app registration. Failed app and action initializations retain their
      pending metadata and can be retried in the same process.
    - removed a stale Zoom webinar-update \c template_id override that synthesized an untyped option absent
      from the supported Meetings schema and prevented snapshot qualification
    - Catalogue protocol 2 detects incompatible Qore module and JS dist installations before registration. Unknown
      app metadata keys produce an actionable \c TYPESCRIPT-CATALOGUE-PROTOCOL-ERROR before typed-hash conversion.
      See \c design/producer-schema-boundary.md and the \c qore-app-schemas manual for deployment details.
    - REST connections accept narrowly typed option hashes, including header-only authentication options.
      Internally added options no longer fail when their value type differs from the caller's options.
    - Fixed adding schema-backed action options with dependencies: option overrides now read the dependency
      list from the option value instead of the iterator record. This supports Trello's additional board/list
      selectors when materializing its current OpenAPI 3 actions.
    - the TypeScript app catalogue settings (\c QORE_TYPESCRIPT_MASTER_ACTION_SCRIPT and
      \c QORE_TYPESCRIPT_ACTION_SCRIPTS) are read from the process environment when the module is initialized, so a
      process can decide not to load the catalogue after it has started, such as a data provider index worker that
      indexes other providers
    - fields do not run their dynamic type or default value callbacks while static metadata is read (see
      \c DataProvider::DataProviderStaticMetadataHelper), so building the data provider index no longer runs them
      without a context, which failed for apps such as Brevo
    - added a versioned TypeScript provider-schema boundary with exact absent/empty/null handling, structurally scoped
      \c AllowedValueInfo conversion, and a lightweight app/action identity inventory for qualified provider-index
      discovery; raw payload hashes containing a \c value member remain opaque, and source failures before identity
      publication remain structural qualification failures until the exact source succeeds
    - a revision mismatch between this module and the TypeScript action script it loads no longer fails
      obscurely in either direction: the action catalogue asserts the registration API it requires before
      registering anything, naming exactly what an older module does not provide, and this module reports an
      action script that predates \c registerDiscoveryInventory() and therefore leaves qualified discovery
      with no exact inventory for its apps. The latter is reported once per action script and retained by
      TypeScriptActionInterface::getIncompleteInventorySources(); such scripts keep working unchanged
    - fixed TypeScriptActionInterface::registerDiscoveryInventory() to accept an app-only identity batch, as
      published for an app with no actions; it previously failed with a runtime type error
    - HubSpot requests optional CMS page and domain-read scopes without adding required CRM installation
      permissions. Its synchronous REST client verifies current token grants before CMS calls and reports
      actionable capability and account-entitlement errors. Existing connections need reauthorization to
      expand their grant; see \c docs/hubspot-cms-oauth.md for deployment and recovery instructions
      (<a href="https://github.com/qoretechnologies/qore/issues/5443">issue 5443</a>)
    - added generic \c TypeScriptAppRestClient::introspectOAuth2Token() for direct or signed
      alternate-service token metadata requests without changing token state. HubSpot CMS checks use
      this API; alternate services must implement the operation described in
      \c docs/oauth2-token-introspection.md
    - copied TypeScript REST clients preserve their owning connection, specialized client behavior,
      and the alternate OAuth endpoint signer and signature header
    - fixed the source-owned provider i18n catalogs shipped in
      \c qlib/TypeScriptActionInterface/i18n to contain exactly the apps and actions registered by
      this module. Catalog generation is scoped to the technical source owner, so installed or
      transitive provider modules cannot add their presentation strings; source-tree validation also
      rejects missing and orphaned catalog domains. Because this module's apps are registered
      \a pending and initialized on demand, correct owner scoping requires the \c DataProvider 3.7
      fix for modules loaded from a deferred app initialization; without it the \c WebSockets app
      (\c WebSocketClient) and the Slack \c watch-messages action (Qorus \c QorusSlackServices) are
      attributed to this module wherever they are installed. Catalogs can be regenerated
      deterministically with \c test/docker_test/update-i18n.sh
    - added lazy, on-demand app loading: instead of eagerly loading every app (and its SDK) when the
      module is loaded, apps are registered \a pending from the data provider index and each app's
      implementation is loaded only on first use (via the catalogue, connection scheme, or data
      provider tree); this is transparent to API users and significantly reduces the memory used by
      the @ref typescriptproxyintro "ts-proxy" layer. A directory&lt;-&gt;app-name map (\c ts-app-dirs.yaml)
      is written next to the app directory during a full load (e.g. \c "qctl update-index") and read at
      runtime to register apps pending from the index; if it is unavailable the module falls back to a
      full load
    - fixed a race where a command could fail with a fatal \c SOCKET-NOT-OPEN error when the command
      IPC socket to the @ref typescriptproxyintro "ts-proxy" child was closed while the child process was
      still running (more likely under load, such as the lazy-load latency of a first app call): the
      proxy now restarts the child and retries the command instead of surfacing the socket error to
      the caller
    - added @ref TypeScriptActionInterface::JavaScriptInProcessPool "JavaScriptInProcessPool" class for
      concurrent in-process JavaScript execution without IPC overhead
      (<a href="https://github.com/qoretechnologies/module-v8/issues/225">issue 225</a>)
    - added @ref TypeScriptActionInterface::InProcessProgramInfo "InProcessProgramInfo" hashdecl
    - added @ref TypeScriptActionInterface::TypeScriptActionInterface::startInProcessServerOnDemand()
      "TypeScriptActionInterface::startInProcessServerOnDemand()" for lazy pool creation with
      configurable maximum pool size
    - added @ref TypeScriptActionInterface::TypeScriptActionInterface::setInProcessServer()
      "TypeScriptActionInterface::setInProcessServer()" for direct pool injection
    - added @ref TypeScriptActionInterface::TypeScriptActionInterface::checkInProcessServer()
      "TypeScriptActionInterface::checkInProcessServer()" for pool access with double-checked locking
    - added @ref TypeScriptActionInterface::TypeScriptActionInterface::shutdownInProcessServer()
      "TypeScriptActionInterface::shutdownInProcessServer()" for safe pool shutdown
    - added clone-mode closure capture mechanism using thread-local
      @ref Priv::PoolCloneModeHelper "PoolCloneModeHelper" to create
      pool programs without modifying global state
    - added static chdir mutex in
      @ref TypeScriptActionInterface::JavaScriptProgramPool "JavaScriptProgramPool" to prevent
      concurrent chdir() races during program creation

    @subsection TypeScriptActionInterface_v1_0 TypeScriptActionInterface v1.0
    - initial release of the module
*/
